1
00:01:24,280 --> 00:01:25,600
I know who you are.

2
00:01:26,280 --> 00:01:27,040
You know me?

3
00:01:28,640 --> 00:01:31,120
You are the daughter of Lu Jingcheng and Yu Wen.

4
00:01:31,880 --> 00:01:32,680
You got it wrong.

5
00:01:33,440 --> 00:01:34,960
Lu Jingcheng is my father,

6
00:01:35,520 --> 00:01:36,600
but my mother

7
00:01:36,920 --> 00:01:38,000
is Annie.

8
00:01:38,520 --> 00:01:40,360
You and the boy from the Lu family

9
00:01:40,360 --> 00:01:41,840
are half-siblings.

10
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:44,480
Annie isn't your biological mother.

11
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:45,680
Back then,

12
00:01:46,320 --> 00:01:47,680
the Lu and An families

13
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:49,520
were joined by marriage for profit.

14
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:51,160
Before they got married,

15
00:01:51,520 --> 00:01:52,440
both of them

16
00:01:52,720 --> 00:01:54,640
had their own lovers.

17
00:01:55,080 --> 00:01:56,400
This marriage

18
00:01:56,600 --> 00:01:57,960
was just a show

19
00:01:58,360 --> 00:01:59,880
from the beginning.

20
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:03,200
After getting married,

21
00:02:03,280 --> 00:02:05,480
they lived their own lives.

22
00:02:05,760 --> 00:02:06,840
[Coincidentally,]

23
00:02:07,160 --> 00:02:10,160
[they both had children with their lovers]

24
00:02:10,320 --> 00:02:12,040
[around the same time,]

25
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:14,080
[and their due dates were close.]

26
00:02:14,600 --> 00:02:16,040
[Unfortunately,]

27
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:18,320
[your birth mother died]

28
00:02:18,640 --> 00:02:20,320
[from amniotic fluid embolism]

29
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:23,200
[during childbirth.]

30
00:02:24,160 --> 00:02:25,160
[Shortly after,]

31
00:02:25,560 --> 00:02:26,440
[your father]

32
00:02:26,640 --> 00:02:28,480
[was diagnosed with advanced lung cancer.]

33
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:29,880
Before he died,

34
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:33,440
he left you 30% of the company's shares

35
00:02:33,880 --> 00:02:36,040
and put them in trust.

36
00:02:36,480 --> 00:02:37,880
When you have a child,

37
00:02:37,880 --> 00:02:40,840
the shares will be transferred back to your name in batches.

38
00:02:41,360 --> 00:02:43,080
And he entrusted you to me.

39
00:02:43,920 --> 00:02:46,120
Not long after your father died,

40
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:47,920
Annie found you.

41
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:50,560
But that woman was too cunning.

42
00:02:50,920 --> 00:02:53,040
She closed the orphanage.

43
00:02:53,280 --> 00:02:56,400
I could only watch you be taken away by her.

44
00:02:57,080 --> 00:02:58,560
I was powerless.

45
00:02:59,160 --> 00:03:01,080
She was afraid that I would tell the truth,

46
00:03:02,360 --> 00:03:04,200
so she forced me to disappear forever.

47
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:07,320
I went to a foreign country.

48
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:08,040
You're lying.

49
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:09,800
What evidence do you have?

50
00:03:10,360 --> 00:03:12,440
You have a plum birthmark on your waist,

51
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:14,880
which is exactly the same as your mother's.

52
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:16,800
Five years ago,

53
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:19,320
a girl named Su Muchen

54
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:22,320
took all your adoption papers from me.

55
00:03:22,840 --> 00:03:24,320
Didn't she show you?

56
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:29,640
Is what she said true?

57
00:03:30,320 --> 00:03:33,000
Building 6, Family Compound 23, Chemical Fiber Factory.

58
00:03:33,680 --> 00:03:35,640
It's Su Muchen's studio.

59
00:03:36,480 --> 00:03:38,240
The documents of the Sunlight Welfare House

60
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:39,800
were taken by Su Muchen

61
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:42,200
from Dean Li.

62
00:03:43,680 --> 00:03:45,360
Su Muchen is still alive.

63
00:03:46,440 --> 00:03:47,600
No way.

64
00:03:48,760 --> 00:03:50,080
Who is Purple Vine?

65
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:51,600
Annie adopted me

66
00:03:51,920 --> 00:03:54,720
because of the 30% shares I inherited.

67
00:03:55,880 --> 00:03:58,600
My shares have already been diluted by 15%.

68
00:04:00,360 --> 00:04:02,800
If all my shares are diluted,

69
00:04:03,800 --> 00:04:04,680
how can I survive

70
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:06,640
in the Lu family with nothing?

71
00:04:46,680 --> 00:04:47,560
Who?

72
00:04:48,160 --> 00:04:49,040
Who's there?

73
00:05:15,280 --> 00:05:16,640
Ah!

74
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:19,800
Jiang Li!

75
00:05:21,400 --> 00:05:22,200
Jiang Li!

76
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:30,680
Bats!

77
00:05:30,720 --> 00:05:32,080
There are bats in the living room.

78
00:05:33,400 --> 00:05:34,160
I hit it with a book

79
00:05:35,880 --> 00:05:37,560
just now.

80
00:05:41,560 --> 00:05:42,000
It's okay.

81
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:48,440
It's okay.

82
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:19,680
The payment is 31.8 yuan.

83
00:06:26,880 --> 00:06:28,640
It should have hurt its wing.

84
00:06:29,200 --> 00:06:31,560
I didn't expect you to be afraid of such a small thing.

85
00:06:31,560 --> 00:06:32,880
In the dark,

86
00:06:33,040 --> 00:06:35,000
who can tell if it's a parrot or a bat?

87
00:06:38,640 --> 00:06:40,600
But why are you in front of my house?

88
00:06:41,040 --> 00:06:42,360
Because I live next door.

89
00:06:43,680 --> 00:06:44,920
When did you move here?

90
00:06:45,160 --> 00:06:46,240
I live in 1801.

91
00:06:46,240 --> 00:06:47,760
I should have moved in

92
00:06:48,400 --> 00:06:51,120
earlier than you.

93
00:06:51,120 --> 00:06:52,280
500 yuan,

94
00:06:52,280 --> 00:06:53,240
12 days.

95
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:56,120
You knew I lived here.

96
00:06:57,840 --> 00:07:00,000
It's really special for you

97
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:01,560
to know your neighbors.

98
00:07:03,440 --> 00:07:04,240
Stop it.

99
00:07:04,400 --> 00:07:04,920
I...

100
00:07:05,240 --> 00:07:06,120
I just knew it.

101
00:07:08,880 --> 00:07:10,440
You're really not good at lying.

102
00:07:11,640 --> 00:07:12,480
But what are we going to do

103
00:07:13,160 --> 00:07:14,400
with it later?

104
00:07:15,160 --> 00:07:16,720
You can only wait until it recovers

105
00:07:17,360 --> 00:07:18,160
and then release it.

106
00:07:18,440 --> 00:07:19,120
No, no, no.

107
00:07:19,280 --> 00:07:20,560
I can't keep pets.

108
00:07:21,400 --> 00:07:23,320
You hurt it with a book.

109
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:25,280
Whether it's fate

110
00:07:25,880 --> 00:07:26,840
or a debt,

111
00:07:27,520 --> 00:07:28,840
you have to take responsibility.

112
00:07:32,800 --> 00:07:33,840
Why don't you keep it?

113
00:07:33,880 --> 00:07:34,560
I...

114
00:07:35,280 --> 00:07:36,920
I'll be moving into the Lu family's house in a few days.

115
00:07:36,920 --> 00:07:37,720
I don't have time to take care of it.

116
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:45,600
Fine.

117
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:47,000
Then give it a name.

118
00:07:47,360 --> 00:07:48,840
I'm not very good at this.

119
00:07:50,400 --> 00:07:51,440
You do it.

120
00:07:54,880 --> 00:07:56,240
Then I'll call it Momo.

121
00:07:56,680 --> 00:07:57,680
You're Young Master Shen,

122
00:07:57,680 --> 00:07:58,680
and it's Momo.

123
00:07:58,880 --> 00:08:00,080
You two make a good roommate.

124
00:08:02,440 --> 00:08:02,880
Okay.

125
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:06,160
It's my treat today.

126
00:08:20,760 --> 00:08:22,120
You're moving into the Lu family?

127
00:08:24,480 --> 00:08:25,160
Yeah.

128
00:08:25,440 --> 00:08:27,440
That's how you win over a playboy's heart,

129
00:08:27,560 --> 00:08:28,400
and avoid being dumped.

130
00:08:29,440 --> 00:08:31,560
Are you really going to marry a scum like Lu Xu?

131
00:08:32,960 --> 00:08:33,760
Or what?

132
00:08:34,320 --> 00:08:35,520
At least he's young,

133
00:08:35,800 --> 00:08:36,840
not some old guy who can't even walk.

134
00:08:36,920 --> 00:08:38,080
You have plenty of choices.

135
00:08:38,080 --> 00:08:39,240
Why choose this?

136
00:08:43,120 --> 00:08:44,480
I know the path I've taken,

137
00:08:45,080 --> 00:08:46,280
and I know where the future lies.

138
00:08:46,560 --> 00:08:47,720
I'm not a princess,

139
00:08:47,920 --> 00:08:49,800
and I don't expect a prince charming.

140
00:08:50,160 --> 00:08:50,800
So,

141
00:08:52,640 --> 00:08:54,560
I won't expect a gentleman

142
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:56,160
like you.

143
00:08:56,400 --> 00:08:57,720
How do you know if you don't try?

144
00:09:05,960 --> 00:09:06,920
Don't joke with me.

145
00:09:06,920 --> 00:09:08,160
I'm not joking.

146
00:09:15,640 --> 00:09:16,320
Come on.

147
00:09:16,520 --> 00:09:17,520
The food is getting cold.

148
00:10:18,240 --> 00:10:19,760
Are you leaving again after this?

149
00:10:20,560 --> 00:10:21,360
Or what?

150
00:10:22,600 --> 00:10:23,760
Today is my birthday.

151
00:10:26,800 --> 00:10:28,040
Happy birthday.

152
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:32,000
That's it?

153
00:10:34,560 --> 00:10:35,320
What else?

154
00:10:36,200 --> 00:10:38,280
I hope you can give me a gift.

155
00:10:50,880 --> 00:10:52,200
Only today,

156
00:10:54,680 --> 00:10:56,080
I hope you can

157
00:10:56,800 --> 00:10:59,000
not treat me as a substitute for her,

158
00:11:17,800 --> 00:11:19,080
and love me once.

159
00:11:28,240 --> 00:11:29,600
If you are not a substitute,

160
00:11:32,800 --> 00:11:34,240
you are nothing.

161
00:12:02,680 --> 00:12:03,880
Honey, you're back.

162
00:12:04,040 --> 00:12:04,960
Are you tired today?

163
00:12:05,880 --> 00:12:06,840
When did you come back?

164
00:12:07,240 --> 00:12:08,080
I just got back today.

165
00:12:08,240 --> 00:12:08,600
Hey.

166
00:12:11,080 --> 00:12:11,960
I can do it myself.

167
00:12:13,920 --> 00:12:14,520
What?

168
00:12:15,040 --> 00:12:16,120
I haven't been back for a few days.

169
00:12:16,360 --> 00:12:18,080
I just missed you.

170
00:12:19,480 --> 00:12:20,400
Do you miss me?

171
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:22,800
Of course.

172
00:12:24,120 --> 00:12:25,720
I made you bird's nest porridge.

173
00:12:25,720 --> 00:12:26,840
I'll bring it to you.

174
00:12:27,640 --> 00:12:28,280
Honey,

175
00:12:33,600 --> 00:12:34,440
did something happen

176
00:12:35,400 --> 00:12:36,200
in Singapore?

177
00:12:37,200 --> 00:12:38,000
No.

178
00:12:38,280 --> 00:12:38,960
What's wrong?

179
00:12:41,400 --> 00:12:42,360
Just asking.

180
00:12:49,440 --> 00:12:50,760
I met a friend

181
00:12:51,040 --> 00:12:52,120
in Singapore.

182
00:12:52,440 --> 00:12:53,840
He said something

183
00:12:54,280 --> 00:12:55,360
I think

184
00:12:55,640 --> 00:12:56,840
he's right.

185
00:12:57,680 --> 00:12:59,360
Love is not always passionate.

186
00:12:59,640 --> 00:13:01,040
It's a lamp in the night,

187
00:13:01,160 --> 00:13:02,520
a glass of water in the morning.

188
00:13:03,720 --> 00:13:05,440
We've carried the bitterness of life together,

189
00:13:05,840 --> 00:13:07,720
and tasted the sweetness of life together.

190
00:13:08,160 --> 00:13:09,560
As long as we hold hands,

191
00:13:10,040 --> 00:13:11,240
we can keep going.

192
00:13:12,040 --> 00:13:13,320
Although we are husband and wife,

193
00:13:13,840 --> 00:13:14,760
we are also each other's

194
00:13:14,760 --> 00:13:16,160
most trusted comrades

195
00:13:16,520 --> 00:13:17,560
and eternal destination.

196
00:13:18,160 --> 00:13:19,200
In the past,

197
00:13:19,520 --> 00:13:21,520
you have endured a lot of my whims,

198
00:13:21,680 --> 00:13:23,800
and silently contributed a lot to this family.

199
00:13:24,160 --> 00:13:25,760
But after the wedding, I realized

200
00:13:26,400 --> 00:13:28,520
I should be a virtuous wife

201
00:13:29,040 --> 00:13:30,000
and a good mother.

202
00:13:31,480 --> 00:13:33,160
I will be your harbor.

203
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:35,160
From now on,

204
00:13:36,120 --> 00:13:37,880
as long as we hold hands,

205
00:13:39,400 --> 00:13:40,600
we'll keep moving forward,

206
00:13:40,920 --> 00:13:41,360
right?

207
00:13:42,800 --> 00:13:43,640
You should get some rest.

208
00:13:43,960 --> 00:13:44,800
I'll bring the bird's nest soup

209
00:13:45,120 --> 00:13:45,960
to the bedroom.

210
00:13:46,520 --> 00:13:47,040
Okay.

211
00:13:54,880 --> 00:13:56,200
Honey, hurry up...

212
00:14:30,240 --> 00:14:31,440
Li,

213
00:14:32,120 --> 00:14:33,680
you finally moved into the old house.

214
00:14:34,160 --> 00:14:35,960
You came back from Singapore so soon.

215
00:14:38,720 --> 00:14:39,960
I was worried about you,

216
00:14:39,960 --> 00:14:41,280
so I came back early.

217
00:14:41,560 --> 00:14:42,440
I brought you a gift.

218
00:14:54,800 --> 00:14:56,360
What a beautiful dress.

219
00:14:57,360 --> 00:14:59,040
It's like tailor-made for me.

220
00:15:00,560 --> 00:15:01,880
Go prepare the tea and snacks.

221
00:15:08,480 --> 00:15:09,520
How did it go?

222
00:15:09,760 --> 00:15:10,480
Don't worry.

223
00:15:10,680 --> 00:15:12,000
It's all taken care of.

224
00:15:12,240 --> 00:15:13,200
Those women

225
00:15:13,560 --> 00:15:15,520
will have no ties with brother-in-law.

226
00:15:16,120 --> 00:15:17,160
I trust you.

227
00:15:17,320 --> 00:15:18,400
You can do it.

228
00:15:19,200 --> 00:15:20,240
Try it on.

229
00:15:20,480 --> 00:15:21,160
Okay.

230
00:15:41,480 --> 00:15:43,080
So many Tiff accessories.

231
00:15:43,480 --> 00:15:45,160
You seem to like this brand.

232
00:15:46,120 --> 00:15:49,040
Because it never caters to fashion trends,

233
00:15:49,520 --> 00:15:52,000
but pursues simple and elegant lines

234
00:15:52,520 --> 00:15:53,800
and timeless beauty.

235
00:15:58,920 --> 00:16:00,680
Clive Kristin perfume.

236
00:16:00,720 --> 00:16:01,960
You like this perfume, too?

237
00:16:02,080 --> 00:16:02,720
Yes.

238
00:16:03,240 --> 00:16:05,800
Because even if it's the same model and the same perfume,

239
00:16:05,920 --> 00:16:07,360
it will be adjusted to a different scent

240
00:16:07,440 --> 00:16:08,920
according to different people.

241
00:16:10,960 --> 00:16:11,920
The point is

242
00:16:12,200 --> 00:16:14,080
it will never be the same as others.

243
00:16:15,120 --> 00:16:16,400
What's the scent of yours?

244
00:16:21,720 --> 00:16:23,280
Clive Kristin.

245
00:16:23,520 --> 00:16:24,560
No.1.

246
00:16:25,600 --> 00:16:26,680
Mine is not the same

247
00:16:26,840 --> 00:16:28,160
from the others.

248
00:16:28,840 --> 00:16:30,760
It has a hint of bitterness

249
00:16:31,160 --> 00:16:32,200
and despair.

250
00:16:37,960 --> 00:16:38,760
How is it?

251
00:16:39,480 --> 00:16:40,280
Does it look good?

252
00:16:42,120 --> 00:16:42,960
Perfect.

253
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:45,000
It's simply

254
00:16:45,520 --> 00:16:47,560
tailor-made for you.
